    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's not that kind of love. It's a debt. A debt that can't be paid with apologies or \"trying to do better\" next time. The men are gone, and the honor is gone with them. In the old songs, when a commander fails this badly, when they've stained their name so deeply... they don't just keep living and pretending. They find a way to balance the scales. They find a way to meet their end with the dignity they lost in the field. It's the only thing left that feels like it might actually mean something.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
